1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,213
Worked example eight point one.

2
00:00:02,213 --> 00:00:10,312
Bromomethane is a methyl halide, so S N two, with rate equals k times both concentrations.

3
00:00:10,312 --> 00:00:18,177
k is two times ten to the minus four over zero point one times zero point one: two times ten to the minus two.

4
00:00:18,177 --> 00:00:23,281
Doubling hydroxide doubles the rate, to four times ten to the minus four.

5
00:00:23,281 --> 00:00:32,565
But for the tertiary halide, the mechanism is S N one, hydroxide is not in the rate law, and doubling it changes nothing.

